<p id="mntl-sc-block_23-0" class="comp mntl-sc-block mntl-sc-block-html"> Outlook is Microsoft&#39;s free email service, offering a solid interface that&#39;s easy to navigate. In my experience, it competes closely with Gmail as one of the best free email providers.
</p>
<p id="mntl-sc-block_24-0" class="comp mntl-sc-block mntl-sc-block-html"> The website is intuitive; right-clicking an email reveals options to move, delete, or search for all messages from a specific sender.
</p>
<p id="mntl-sc-block_25-0" class="comp mntl-sc-block mntl-sc-block-html"> Outlook supports mail rules, which means you can set new messages to move to a specified folder automatically and be categorized, flagged, or forwarded if certain conditions are met.
</p>
